{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/55859-patchwork-covers","id":55859,"title":"Patchwork covers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-22T18:02:31-08:00","id":55859,"title":"Patchwork covers","content":"Thoughts on what a Cover made fresh would look like? could you decide based on the lives you add? based off the first pact? pick and choose as you go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2001-tyler-foss","name":"Tyler Foss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T18:42:21-08:00","id":55882,"title":"","content":"As far as i knew that was the point. you make pacts and custom craft your cover. it is suppose to feel more natural and more 'you' to the demon when i read it so i'd simply say yes :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2040-sootfeathers","name":"SootFeathers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T21:23:50-08:00","id":55933,"title":"","content":"I suspect it'd look physically like an agglomeration of all the people whose lives you used to make it. If you've ever read the animorphs books, think about how Ax made a new &quot;human&quot; morph by acquiring the patterns of all 5 of his friends and synthesizing them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T09:44:49-08:00","id":56197,"title":"","content":"I'll assume you're talking about the physical appearance. I'd look at the patches and what telltale effects they would have. A history with alcoholism would lead to sullen eyes and potentially liver spots, a battle with drugs would leave faint track marks, an abusive spouse would leave healed fractures/cigarette burns/scars, a job as a construction worker would leave callused and muscular hands, a Jewish heritage would make you be circumcised, taking someone's cancer would leave the targeting tattoos/baldness (assuming chemo) and surgical scars. Adding on patches to an established Cover would make these signs appear over a day or so, while a just-formed Patchwork Cover would start out with these.<br /> <br /> Beyond the telltales, it's up to the individual Demon to decide how they're stitched together. Hair color, gender, height, eye color, home, job, wardrobe, friends.... If they're not set by the patches, it's up to the Demon to decide or create them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/55859-patchwork-covers?p=55933#post55933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect it'd 